From c8b006000aa639919e88608601fa22661a188be8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giorgos Sarigiannidis <contact@gsarigiannidis.gr>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:09:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Mark changed words, not characters, and ignore whitespace

Inline highlighting compared character by character and drew whitespace
inside highlights, so a re-indented block marked every added space and
line break with dots and arrows. Compare words and punctuation instead,
never whitespace, and mark a run of changed words as one span. A stray
matching '?' or '(' on one line no longer splits a change in pieces.

Conflict chunks with lines on both sides get the same word marks;
before, only plain changes did. Whitespace glyphs are no longer drawn
inside highlights.
